 "text": "Hello there! How's your day treating you? Lots of laptops come with good left-handed support these days, it' worth checking the manual if you' not already using one. Not on the go, but for sitting at a desk. A thin case with a pad and a trackpad cover can work wonders. MacBook Pro is the classic one. It has full size keys between the fingers for quick shooting without looking, and you can use it one handed for quick searches. Some mid to high range desktops also come with them. Look for a trackpad with a wide face that doesn't dig in, and a case with a pad.",
